:: Hospital XChange Therapy Ask
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
You explain that you've been dosed with X-Change pills against your will, and that you've heard rumours of a treatment,
a course of injections, that can keep the drug from taking hold. You ask whether <<he>> could provide it.
<br><br>
Harper sets <<his>> clipboard down and frowns.
"And why," <<he>> says slowly, "would you think I'd give you something like that?"
<br><br>
You get the distinct feeling you've touched on something you shouldn't have.
Still, you've come this far. How do you press your case?
<br><br>
<<link [[Say you only want to feel safe in your own body again|Hospital XChange Therapy Debate Plead]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Offer to pay whatever it costs|Hospital XChange Therapy Debate Money]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Argue that helping you is a doctor's duty|Hospital XChange Therapy Debate Duty]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy Debate Plead
<<effects>>
"Please," you say. "People keep drugging me against my will. I just want to feel safe in my own body again."
<br><br>
<<He>> studies you for a long moment, and something almost like sympathy crosses <<his>> face,
though it doesn't quite reach <<his>> eyes. "I understand it's distressing.
But what you're describing isn't a recognised treatment. As far as the world is concerned, it doesn't exist.
I can't simply prescribe something that doesn't exist."
<br><br>
The careful way <<he>> phrases it, "as far as the world is concerned", doesn't escape you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Beg for help one more time|Hospital XChange Therapy Refused]]>><<set $xchange.therapy.debatePath to "beg">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Insist the treatment exists and that the doctor knows what it is|Hospital XChange Therapy Refused]]>><<set $xchange.therapy.debatePath to "probe">><</link>>
<br>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy Debate Money
<<effects>>
"I can pay," you press. "Whatever it costs, I'll find the money. Just name it."
<br><br>
"This isn't about money," <<he>> says. Then, after a pause, "Or rather, it isn't only about money.
There are... considerations. It isn't mine to give." 
<br><br>
<<He>> doesn't explain what <<he>> means, and clearly doesn't intend to.
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask whose decision it really is|Hospital XChange Therapy Refused]]>><<set $xchange.therapy.debatePath to "whose">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse to leave without it|Hospital XChange Therapy Refused]]>><<set $xchange.therapy.debatePath to "price">><</link>>
<br>


:: Hospital XChange Therapy Debate Duty
<<effects>>
"You're a doctor," you say. "This is hurting me, and you can stop it. Isn't that your whole job?"
<br><br>
"My job..." <<he>> repeats, very quietly. "Yes. I do try to remember what my job is supposed to be.
But there's nothing I can do for you here."
<br><br>
<<link [[Lose your temper|Hospital XChange Therapy Refused]]>><<set $xchange.therapy.debatePath to "angry">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Apologise and admit you're frightened|Hospital XChange Therapy Refused]]>><<set $xchange.therapy.debatePath to "apologise">><</link>>
<br>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy Refused
<<effects>>
<<switch $xchange.therapy.debatePath>>
<<case "beg">>
	You beg, your voice cracking.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> seems almost wavers, you're sure of it, but then <<his>> expression closes like a door.
	"No. Please don't make this harder than it has to be."
<<case "probe">>
	"It exists," you insist. "And you know exactly what it is, don't you?" 
	<br><br>
	"Be careful asking questions like that. For your own sake." What <<he>> say sounds like genuine concern.
<<case "whose">>
	"Then whose decision is it?" you demand. "Who do I have to ask?"
	<br><br>
	"That's not something you want to know," <<he>> says flatly. "And not something I can tell you. Leave it alone."
<<case "price">>
	You plant yourself in the chair and tell <<him>> you're not leaving without it.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "You don't understand. There isn't a number. It's not for sale. I'm sorry."
<<case "angry">>
	Your temper snaps and your voice rises.
	<br><br>
	"You're upset. That's understandable." <<He>> picks <<his>> clipboard back up, a clear signal that the conversation is over.
	"But raising your voice won't change anything, and it could make things worse for you. I'd advise you to let this go."
<<case "apologise">>
	You quietly admit how frightened you are.
	<br><br>
	"It's alright," <<he>> says. "Anyone would be. But being frightened doesn't change what I can and can't do."
<<default>>
	<<He>> simply shakes <<his>> head.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
No matter how you frame it, Harper won't budge. Whatever this treatment is, and whoever it really belongs to,
<<he>> has no intention of giving it to you. <span class="red">You leave the office empty-handed.</span><<gstress>><<gtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Hospital Foyer]]>>
	<<set $xchange.therapy.questStage to 1>><<set $xchange.therapy.refusedDay to Time.days>>
	<<unset $xchange.therapy.debatePath>><<stress 6>><<trauma 3>><<endevent>>
<</link>>
<br>

:: Harper Therapy Decline
<<set $outside to 1>><<effects>>
<<He>> nods. "Of course. Come to my office at the hospital whenever you'd like to start, and I'll explain everything.
I'll be expecting you."
<br><br>
With that, <<he>> turns and walks back the way <<he>> came.
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.therapy.questStage to 2>>
<<endevent>>
<<destinationeventend>>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy Explain
<<effects>><<endevent>>
<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
<<if $xchange.therapy.questStage lt 3>>
	Harper leads you through to <<his>> office and closes the door.
	The wariness <<he>> showed when you first asked about this is gone, replaced by something more businesslike.
	<br><br>
	"Let me explain how this works," <<he>> says. "The drug you keep being dosed with is... persistent.
	I can't simply make you immune. What I can do is run a course of treatment that keeps your body from latching onto any new dose for a set window of time.
	While the treatment holds, nothing new will take. Anything already in your system has to run its course on its own, I'm afraid."
	<br><br>
	"It's expensive," <<he>> continues, "and it's a great deal of work on my end.
	This isn't the kind of thing one can simply... avoid, normally. So you need to understand the price.
	You can come to me whenever you'd like to start a window, here, at this office."
	<br><br>
	<<set $xchange.therapy.questStage to 3>>
<<else>>
	"Back again," Harper says. "Let's see about your treatment."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<include "Hospital XChange Therapy Menu">>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy
<<effects>><<endevent>>
<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
"What can I do for you?" Harper asks.
<br><br>
<<include "Hospital XChange Therapy Menu">>

:: Widgets XChange Therapy [widget]
<<widget "xchange-therapy-prices">>
	/* central definition of the three windows: [label, hours, cost-in-pennies, display] */
	<<set _therapyOptions to [
		["1 day", 24, 1000000, "&pound;10,000"],
		["1 week", 168, 5000000, "&pound;50,000"],
		["1 month", 720, 15000000, "&pound;150,000"]
	]>>
<</widget>>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy Menu
<<xchange-therapy-prices>>
<<if $xchange.therapy.active and $xchange.therapy.countdown gt 0>>
	<<set _hoursLeft to Math.ceil($xchange.therapy.countdown)>>
	<<set _daysLeft to Math.floor(_hoursLeft / 24)>>
	<span class="blue">You're currently under the cleansing treatment.</span> It will protect you against being pilled for roughly
	<<if _daysLeft gte 1>>another <<print _daysLeft>> day<<if _daysLeft isnot 1>>s<</if>><<if (_hoursLeft % 24) gt 0>> and <<print (_hoursLeft % 24)>> hour<<if (_hoursLeft % 24) isnot 1>>s<</if>><</if>><<else>>another <<print _hoursLeft>> hour<<if _hoursLeft isnot 1>>s<</if>><</if>>.
	<br><br>
	"There's no sense starting another course while this one's still working," Harper says. "Come back when it wears off."
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	Harper outlines the options. The longer you want to stay clean, the more it costs.
	<br><br>
	<<for _opt range _therapyOptions>>
		<<capture _opt>>
			<<if $money gte (setup.inflation ? setup.inflation.price(_opt[2]) : _opt[2])>>
				<<pillicon "blue">><<link `"Stay clean for " + _opt[0] + " (" + (setup.inflation ? formatMoney(setup.inflation.price(_opt[2])) : _opt[3]) + ")"`>>
					<<set $xchange.therapy.active to true>>
					<<set $xchange.therapy.duration to _opt[1]>>
					<<set $xchange.therapy.countdown to _opt[1]>>
					<<money `-_opt[2]` "xchangeTherapy">>
					<<goto "Hospital XChange Therapy Done">>
				<</link>>
			<<else>>
				<<pillicon "blue">><span class="gray">Stay clean for <<print _opt[0]>> (<<print (setup.inflation ? formatMoney(setup.inflation.price(_opt[2])) : _opt[3])>>)</span> <span class="red">You can't afford it.</span>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</capture>>
	<</for>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hospital XChange Therapy Done
<<effects>>
<<set _hoursLeft to Math.ceil($xchange.therapy.countdown)>>
<<set _daysLeft to Math.round(_hoursLeft / 24)>>
Harper accepts the payment and leads you to a treatment room. The course takes the better part of two hours,
a series of injections and checks, and leaves you feeling faintly sore but clear-headed.
<br><br>
"That should hold for <<if _daysLeft gte 1>>about <<print _daysLeft>> day<<if _daysLeft isnot 1>>s<</if>><<else>>a day<</if>>,"
<<he>> says, dabbing the last injection site. "<span class="blue">While it lasts, no new dose will take hold.</span>
Anything already working its way through you will have to finish on its own. Come back if you need another course."
<<lstress>><<gpain>><<pass 2 hours>><<stress -6>><<pain 4>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hospital Dance Injury Treatment
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
A nurse examines your <<if $danceStudio.training.injury is "hard">>injured leg<<else>>sore feet<</if>>, treats the strained muscles and shows you how to support them while they recover. After an hour, you can move comfortably again.
<<set $danceStudio.training.injury to "none">><<set $danceStudio.training.injuryUntil to 0>>
<br><br>
<span class="green">Your dance injury has healed.</span>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Hospital Parasite Chastity Public
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>

<<upperstrip>>
<<lowerstrip>>
<<underlowerstrip>>
<<underupperstrip>>
"Please undress," Harper says as <<he>> stands to leave the room. You remove what you can, though your $worn.genitals.name stays locked in place. <<He>> soon returns, carrying a medical gown.
<br><br>
"Wear this," <<he>> instructs. You quickly put the gown on. "Right, if you'd like to come with me, it's just a short walk away."
<br><br>
<<generate2>><<generate3>><<generate4>><<generate5>><<generate6>>
<<He>> leads you to another part of the hospital. Your breath catches when you enter the auditorium. Seats rise up in a circle around a central platform. The audience is far larger than you expected, and people are still entering. Harper smiles at you reassuringly. "Don't be nervous, we'll be done before you know it!"
<br><br>

When the seats are full the lights in the audience dim, and Harper softly speaks. "If you would disrobe and lie on the table, please."
<br>
Your gown falls to the floor, unveiling you and your $worn.genitals.name for the whole audience to see. A murmur runs through the crowd.
<br><br>

You lie on the table as instructed, and shortly after Harper produces straps from the underside of the bed, swiftly subduing your limbs. <<He>> sticks small pads around your $worn.genitals.name. <<He>> takes a seat and turns to a small machine covered in switches and dials.
<br><br>

Once satisfied, <<he>> turns to you. "We're all ready to start, just relax." <<He>> turns back to the device in front of <<him>>. Without further warning, an electric pulse jolts through you.
<br><br>

<<arousal 4000 "genitals">>
<<if $pleasure gte $pleasuremax>><<orgasm>><<hospitalparasite>><</if>>

The pulses increase in intensity. <<He>> produces a pair of heavy-duty cutters. "Going to need to get this off you first," <<he>> says, working the blades in around your $worn.genitals.name. A few tense seconds later, it clatters to the table in pieces.
<br><br>

<<chastityParasiteHospitalCure>>

<<person1>><<He>> switches off the machine and the pulses immediately stop, leaving a mild tingling in their place. <<He>> removes the pads from your body and undoes the straps. "All done! Whatever that was, it's gone now." <<He>> smiles. "You can get dressed."
<br><br>
<<pass 10>>
<<He>> holds the door open for you on your way out. "Be well."
<br><br>
<<endevent>>
<<clotheson>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Hospital Foyer]]>><</link>>
<br><br>

